(* credits_unlinkability.pv - ProVerif model of blind-RSA credit unlinkability
   (docs/VERIFICATION_PLAN.md item 5). Companion to formal/credits/credits.spthy (no double
   spending and issuer-only minting, Tamarin) and tools/mesh_tokens.py.

   PROPERTY: an issuer that sees every issuance cannot tell which issuance a spend came
   from. Two members are each issued one credit; afterwards (phase 1) both credits are
   spent. In one world the spends come in issuance order, in the other swapped; the two
   worlds are observationally equivalent.

   ADVERSARY: the issuer, also running the ledger. It holds the signing key, signs whatever
   it is sent, may answer an issuance with any value it likes, and sees every spend.

   MODELED, as tools/mesh_tokens.py does it: a fresh random token per credit; the member
   blinds the token's full-domain hash (`blind`), the issuer signs the blinded value
   (`sign_blinded`), the member unblinds (`unblind`) and checks the signature under the
   epoch key it trusts before keeping the credit (`unblind` with `token`; RFC 9474
   Finalize); a spend shows the token and the signature (`make_spend`), from which the
   ledger derives its digest. Every member trusts the same published key for the epoch
   (key consistency: `redeem_live` accepts only the published epoch keys).

   ABSTRACTED: RSA blinding and the full-domain hash are the standard blind-signature
   equational theory: unblinding a signature on a blinded message gives the signature on
   the message. Its multiplicative structure is not modelled, so this model cannot show
   the tagging attack that the finalize check stops (an issuer multiplying a blind
   signature by a per-member factor); tools/test_mesh_tokens.py shows that attack against
   the real RSA arithmetic and the check refusing it.

   NOT MODELED: one-more unforgeability (computational, from the RSA blind-signature
   literature) and timing: a credit spent right after it was issued is linkable by time,
   which no blinding hides.

   MUTANTS (edits in tools/proverif_check.py; each must fail to prove):
   - the member sends its token's hash unblinded;
   - each member trusts its own issuer key, which the spend names. *)

free c: channel.

type skey.
type pkey.

fun pk(skey): pkey.
fun fdh(bitstring): bitstring.
fun sign(bitstring, skey): bitstring.
fun blind(bitstring, bitstring): bitstring.
reduc forall m: bitstring, k: skey; checksign(sign(m, k), pk(k)) = m.
reduc forall m: bitstring, r: bitstring; unblind(blind(m, r), r) = m;
      forall m: bitstring, r: bitstring, k: skey; unblind(sign(blind(m, r), k), r) = sign(m, k).

process
  new sk: skey;
  out(c, sk);
  ! (
    new tokenA: bitstring; new rA: bitstring;
    new tokenB: bitstring; new rB: bitstring;
    out(c, blind(fdh(tokenA), rA));
    out(c, blind(fdh(tokenB), rB));
    in(c, signedA: bitstring);
    in(c, signedB: bitstring);
    let sigA = unblind(signedA, rA) in
    let sigB = unblind(signedB, rB) in
    if checksign(sigA, pk(sk)) = fdh(tokenA) then
    if checksign(sigB, pk(sk)) = fdh(tokenB) then
    phase 1;
    out(c, choice[(tokenA, sigA), (tokenB, sigB)]);
    out(c, choice[(tokenB, sigB), (tokenA, sigA)])
  )
